WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:03.540
Speaker 1: Let's go next to.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.610
How about Stevie from Asheville, North Carolina?

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:08.630
Stevie, welcome.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:10.690
Speaker 5: Hey, David.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:11.690
Thanks for having me on.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:12.690
My pleasure.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:16.720
I just had a question, a little bit of a specific
question today.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:18.680
I guess the theme is Supreme Court.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:26.710
But so in the idea of or in counseling, there's
this concept of duty to protect, whereas a

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:33.100
client has confidentiality from their therapist
in most cases, except for a few specific ones,

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.570
and just take to list one.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:36.829
For instance, child abuse.

00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:42.300
If a client were to disclose to a therapist
that they're abusing their child, then duty

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.809
to war and duty to protect the counselor would
have to inform the law.

00:00:45.809 --> 00:00:50.350
Of course, my question is, in the wake of
some of this, in the wake of the Supreme Court

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:55.390
decision in which some states are going to
ban abortion, I'm curious if some states are

00:00:55.390 --> 00:01:03.100
going to say, oh, a fetus that is a child,
if a if a client were to say they're seeking

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.909
an abortion outside of the state, does would
that fall under child abuse?

00:01:07.909 --> 00:01:13.789
And would the counselor have a duty to protect
for an unborn child?

00:01:13.789 --> 00:01:17.920
Speaker 1: So they would absolutely argue
that.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:24.030
I think the question would be whether local
police could really do anything about it,

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:29.219
because let's imagine a different example,
I guess imagine that a client disclosed to

00:01:29.219 --> 00:01:35.719
a client in Texas, disclose to their therapist,
I'm planning to kill someone in Amsterdam

00:01:35.719 --> 00:01:37.159
or something like that.

00:01:37.159 --> 00:01:38.159
Okay.

00:01:38.159 --> 00:01:43.549
So the therapist can go and they can call
Texas police and Texas police maybe could

00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:47.359
ask some questions, but they really probably
can't do anything.

00:01:47.359 --> 00:01:49.329
The crime is supposedly going to happen in
Amsterdam.

00:01:49.329 --> 00:01:53.450
And then if you call Amsterdam police and
say this person might be doing this thing,

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:57.700
they would say, okay, thanks for letting us
know if they come to Amsterdam, then we will

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:58.909
be aware of it.

00:01:58.909 --> 00:02:01.499
But there's nothing they can do until the
person is there.

00:02:01.499 --> 00:02:06.540
So indeed, in thinking about the instance
of, Oh, abortion's banned in Texas, you tell

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:11.909
your therapist I'm going to go to neighboring
wherever to get an abortion.

00:02:11.909 --> 00:02:16.870
I don't think Texas police can really do anything
about it because it's not a crime in that

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.960
other state and they're not planning to do
it in Texas.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:23.830
Yeah, I think that they will make the argument,
but I don't think it will be very effective

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:24.870
at doing anything.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.390
Speaker 5: Right.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:30.950
I think that it all comes back to trying to
enforce abortion laws like this in general

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.060
is just kind of silly.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.280
Speaker 1: Yes, it is.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:34.469
It absolutely is.

00:02:34.469 --> 00:02:39.080
And there are going to be all sorts of absurd
situations like this, for sure.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.400
But we'll have to deal with them as they come
up.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.640
Speaker 5: Right.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:43.890
Okay, well, that.

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:45.880
That's just the thought I've been having lately.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:47.099
Thank you for having me on.

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:48.099
Speaker 1: All right.

00:02:48.099 --> 00:02:49.670
Steve from Asheville, very much appreciate
it.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:50.670
Nice connection.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.129
Got right to the question.

00:02:52.129 --> 00:02:53.610
Hard to beat that.

